    {
      "tag": "h1",
      "text": "Green",
      "box": {
        "x": 779,
        "y": 228,
        "w": 402,
        "h": 46
      },
      "font": "adobe-caslon-w01-smbd, serif",
      "size": "42px",
      "weight": "400",
      "style": "normal",
      "lineHeight": "46.2px",
      "letterSpacing": "normal",
      "color": "rgb(15, 35, 6)",
      "align": "center",
      "transform": "capitalize",
      "decoration": "none"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "My favorite color is the green that leaves turn as the sunlight glows through them. I've thought this since I was a little kid, walking through trails, going camping with my dad, and it still holds true today. Green is my favorite color. It represents life, nature, and a kind of freedom that I only feel when I'm outdoors. I feel so at peace and like myself with the wind blowing in my ears and green all around me. The feeling that I get when I look at nature was my inspiration for this piece. In a way, I feel that that sensation is my essence as a person. I wanted the leaves to have the faint glow of the sun filtered through them, and for the page to be covered in freeform doodles and stars. These are all things that speak to me, and paint that image of freedom, movement, and overwhelming peace.",
      "box": {
        "x": 807,
        "y": 287,
        "w": 346,
        "h": 624
      },
      "font": "alfabet, sans-serif",
      "size": "20px",
      "weight": "400",
      "style": "normal",
      "lineHeight": "26px",
      "letterSpacing": "normal",
      "color": "rgb(15, 35, 6)",
      "align": "start",
      "transform": "none",
      "decoration": "none"
    },
    {
      "tag": "h1",
      "text": "Technical Process",
      "box": {
        "x": 404,
        "y": 1920,
        "w": 480,
        "h": 44
      },
      "font": "adobe-caslon-w01-smbd, serif",
      "size": "40px",
      "weight": "400",
      "style": "normal",
      "lineHeight": "44px",
      "letterSpacing": "normal",
      "color": "rgb(15, 35, 6)",
      "align": "center",
      "transform": "capitalize",
      "decoration": "none"
    },
    {
      "tag": "span",
      "text": "I grabbed a piece of paper, some newspaper, and some rubber cement, and I began to cut out words, pictures, and titles that stuck out to me. I wanted to create a sense of urgency or chaos to symbolize the outside world and the escape that nature offers by literally covering some of the buzzwords. I cut each piece of paper out with an Exacto knife, glued it down, and left it to dry. I then began to paint a picture of a few leaves with light showing through them using acrylic paint. I cut these pieces out as well and set them on top to mark their locations. I then painted and cut out a few stars, and doodled a few freeform shapes on my collage with some markers. I took all of the leaves and stars off and used the printmaking stamps to add some pattern and repetition to make the work look less barren, and some halftone effects to fill the space. I then glued everything on top of it and put it in a frame.",
      "box": {
        "x": 67,
        "y": 1965,
        "w": 1136,
        "h": 206
      },
      "font": "alfabet, sans-serif",
      "size": "20px",
      "weight": "400",
      "style": "normal",
      "lineHeight": "26px",
      "letterSpacing": "normal",
      "color": "rgb(15, 35, 6)",
      "align": "start",
      "transform": "none",
      "decoration": "none"
    },
